In article <1992Nov30.112341.20613@yang.earlham.edu>, davidw@yang.earlham.edu writes...
>1.  I was doing pretty well with a 6th(?) level priest when I descended to 
>level 5 and found about 8 Modor Orcs waiting for me.  I managed to take a 
>few out with a ricocheting Wand of Magic Missle, but they got me anyway.  
>I've gotten down as far as level 8 (with a Tourist!:)) and I've never seen 
>anything like that before or since.  What happened?

Magic Missiles (or anything fired by a wand) can bounce.  This is not at all 
uncommon.  Firing on a diagonal reduces the chance that it will reflect back on 
you.

>2.  I guess my clever cat/dog stole one too many things from one of the 
>shops, becuase it looked like the shop keeper killed it.  Does this happen 
>often?

The only times I've seen a shopkeeper kill a pet is when the pet attacked her
first.  Since pets won't attack thing more powerful than themselves, this won't
happen with a cat/dog (but could with a baby gray dragon).  Also possible if you
were wearing a ring of conflict at the time.

>3.  I've found rings of Teleport and Polymorph, but they don't seem to do 
>anything when I wear them.  How can I tell if I'm polymorphed (other than 
>using a stethescope) and how do I teleport?

You'll know when you polymorph.  If you turn into a monster, your "@" will 
change to the appropriate monster symbol.  Wearing these rings dosen't take 
effect immediatly.  They randomly choose when to polymorph/teleport you.  You
don't have any control over what they do ar when they do it.

>4.  What is a Ring of Combat?

Ain't no such animal.  Maybe you're thinking of a ring of Conflict?  A ring of
conflict will cause monsters to fight each other.  Neat item.

